decide.promptTemplate:
You fly a small drone through a green ring. Each turn is 30 degrees. FORWARD moves 0.5 m. ASCEND and DESCEND move 0.5 m up or down. Towers reach the ceiling, so go around them; coloured boxes are low, so you may climb over them or go around. A collision blocks the move, so the drone stays where it is. Scene description from the camera (written by another model): {{scene}}
Your recent moves, oldest first: {{history}}
Steer toward the target: if the ring is left, TURN_LEFT; if it is right, TURN_RIGHT; if it is above the centre, ASCEND; if it is below the centre, DESCEND; if it is centre and level, FORWARD. If the ring is not visible, TURN_RIGHT to look around. Only if a tower or box is directly ahead (centre) and near, move away from it instead (turn, or ASCEND over a box). Do not zig-zag: do not undo your last turn unless an obstacle forces it. Never reply STOP. Valid actions: FORWARD, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT, ASCEND, DESCEND. Keep your reasoning short. Your reply must end with a final line of exactly this form: ACTION: <WORD>
